  "is_sufficient": false,
  "knowledge_gaps": [
    "The four proposed controls separate the loss from the complete residual, but do not isolate adaptive gating, asymmetric projections, or improvements over the starting scalar recent-mean residual. The originality and potential ratings remain provisional without these comparisons.",
    "With linear source and target projections, the residual equals rᵀW_sourceᵀW_target e_candidate. This is a bilinear model; separate projections alone do not guarantee learned directionality. Projection rescaling can also compensate for gate magnitude, so gate summaries cannot measure branch reliance.",
    "Reproduction details are missing: projection dimensions and initialization, gate architecture, embedding normalization, residual scale, optimizer settings, regularization, loss reduction, and exact causal pooling and prefix-length conventions. A gate bias of -2 alone does not ensure a small initial residual.",
    "The report does not allocate the remaining 43,200 GPU-second budget across controls, diagnostics, and failures, or specify checkpoint selection. Repeated selection on 200 validation users per category risks validation overfitting; the prescribed training seed does not establish robustness across training runs.",
    "Training-only misranking and deletion probes motivate hypotheses but do not establish that stronger recency is beneficial. The proposed branch could learn item popularity or repeated-item shortcuts. Sampled validation HR@10 also does not establish improvement in the simulator's full-catalog recommendations."
  ],
  "follow_up_queries": [
    {
      "reason": "Clarify established precedents and the minimum controls needed to attribute gains to adaptive routing and directionality. This would also ground the originality assessment and prevent interpreting gate magnitude as reliance.",
      "query": "How do FPMC (Factorizing Personalized Markov Chains), FOSSIL (FactOrized Sequential Prediction with Item Similarity Models), and gated short-term/long-term sequential recommenders compare with SASRec scoring hᵀe_j + sigmoid(MLP(h,r,log(1+length))) rᵀAᵀB e_j, where r averages the last three item embeddings? What scalar-gate, fixed-gate, symmetric-bilinear, and parameter-matched ablations distinguish adaptive routing from extra capacity, and how should branch contribution be measured when gate and projection scales are not identifiable?"
    },
    {
      "reason": "Resolve sampling, optimization, and memory details before treating implementation difficulty as moderate. The result should inform an explicit reproducible specification rather than imply an unbiased full-softmax objective.",
      "query": "For SASRec trained at every nonpadding sequence position with candidate-set cross-entropy over one positive and 32 unique uniform negatives sampled without replacement from items outside the user's complete training history, what are reproducible PyTorch sampling and chunked-scoring implementations? How do user-dependent exclusion sets, variable eligible-catalog sizes, loss reduction, embedding norms, and logit temperature affect optimization and comparison with one-negative BCE?"
    },
    {
      "reason": "Strengthen evaluation without changing the pinned evaluator or accessing test labels. Investigate how to distinguish validation-selection noise and popularity shortcuts from evidence supporting the proposed mechanism.",
      "query": "What sequential-recommendation evaluation methods address repeated model selection on a fixed validation set of 200 users per category with 99 sampled negatives, particularly for macro HR@10 across four categories? Consider paired within-category user bootstrap uncertainty conditional on fixed seed 42, prespecified checkpoint and trial selection, equal-compute learning curves, popularity-only and last-item controls, and separate full-catalog recommendation diagnostics; what conclusions remain unsupported by training-history deletion probes?"
    }
  ]
}
